  <data name="RichTextBox1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>There are many components used to make a Program, these are the following:

1. Keywords (also known as Reserved Words)
	- These are words that has special meaning which make up a high-level programming language. These words are not usable for
	any other purpose.

2. Operators
	- Special symbols that perform various operations on data.

3. Variables
	- Used to store data in memory.

4. Syntax
	- These are a set of rules, similar of a spoken language such as, English, but must be strictly followed. If even a single syntax error
	appears in a program, it will not compile or execute.

5. Statements
	- The instructions made up of keywords, variables, and operators. These are also called "Source Code" or simply "Code."

6. Procedures
	- A set of programming statements that performs a specific task.

7. Comments (or Remarks)
	- Part of a program that are ignored when ran. This helps a human reader to understand the pupose of programming statements.
	In Visual Basic, any statement that begins with an Apostrophe ( ' ), will turn green, meaning that the statement that follows are
	comments or remarks.</value>
